# Package-local dependency information for the private libraries.
#
# Why this file has to exist at all: debian/rules skips dh_makeshlibs
# entirely, deliberately -- a shipped shlibs file would advertise this package
# as a system-wide provider of libindiclient.so.2 and friends, which is
# precisely the shadowing this project exists to prevent. But dpkg-shlibdeps
# still refuses to finish while any linked library has no dependency
# information, and every driver in indi-stable-core links libindidriver.so.2.
# Those two requirements collide, and this file is what resolves them.
#
# debian/shlibs.local is the right instrument because it is consulted FIRST,
# ahead of every other source (dpkg-shlibdeps(1), "Shlibs files"), and is
# never installed into any binary package -- it exists only for the duration
# of the build. Nothing outside this source tree can ever resolve a
# dependency through it.
#
# The alternative, --ignore-missing-info, was rejected: it suppresses the
# error for ALL libraries, including system ones, turning a build failure
# into a silently under-specified dependency. Naming our four libraries
# explicitly keeps that failure mode intact for anything else.
#
# The bare package name, with no version relation, is deliberate. The strict
# indi-stable-core-libs (= ${binary:Version}) lives in debian/control where a
# substvar can actually be expanded; shlibs entries take literal text only,
# so a version here would have to be hand-edited every release and would go
# stale silently.
#
# SONAME versions below were read from the built artifacts with readelf -d,
# not inferred from the filenames.
libindidriver 2 indi-stable-core-libs
libindiclient 2 indi-stable-core-libs
libindiAlignmentDriver 2 indi-stable-core-libs
libindilx200 2 indi-stable-core-libs
